CORE
IfaceDispatch
--function IfaceDispatch.test --java-load-classpath-implementations --unwind 3 -cp target/classes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR
^.*FAILURE$
^.*no body for callee
--
Regression for Item B: virtual dispatch through interface
entry-point parameters with --java-load-classpath-implementations.

The test class IfaceDispatch.test takes a Greeter g (interface)
and calls g.greet(). With --java-load-classpath-implementations:
- enumerate_classpath_classes scans the classpath JARs/dirs
- Hello and Bye (concrete implementations) are auto-loaded
- select_pointer_typet::get_parameter_alternative_types walks
  the class hierarchy and returns Hello, Bye as alternatives
- ci_lazy_methodst::initialize_instantiated_classes seeds these
  as instantiable so their greet() method bodies are reachable
- The entry-point harness emits a nondet-switch that allocates
  a Hello or Bye object
- remove_virtual_functions resolves g.greet() to either
  Hello.greet() or Bye.greet()

The assertion `r == 1 || r == 2` succeeds because both
implementations return one of those values.
